---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
const REPO = "https://github.com/daviddef/TheFalco";
import sources from "../data/sources.json";
const groups = [...new Set(sources.map(s => s.g))];
---
<Base title="Sources">
  <h1>Sources</h1>
  <p class="lede">What has been read, where it is, and what it actually established. Fifteen sources
  across four countries' worth of record-keeping, and the repository files that carry every citation.</p>

  {groups.map(g => (
    <section>
      <h2>{g}</h2>
      {sources.filter(s => s.g === g).map(s => (
        <div class="card" style="margin:.9rem 0">
          <h3 style="margin-bottom:.35rem">{s.t}</h3>
          <p style="margin:.2rem 0 .5rem">{s.d}</p>
          {s.id !== "—" ? <p class="small mono" style="margin:.2rem 0">{s.id}</p> : null}
          <p class="small" style="margin:.35rem 0 0"><strong>What it established:</strong> {s.use}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </section>
  ))}

  <h2>The underlying files</h2>
  <p>Every claim on this site resolves to a row in one of three files. They are plain tab-separated
  text, kept in the repository so that anyone can check the working rather than take it on trust.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={REPO + "/blob/main/data/record-citations.tsv"}><strong>record-citations.tsv</strong></a>
    — <strong>33</strong> record citations: archival reference, collection, event, date, place, subject
    and the named parent or spouse.</li>
    <li><a href={REPO + "/blob/main/data/households.tsv"}><strong>households.tsv</strong></a>
    — <strong>52</strong> register entries behind the households, each with the quoted words of the
    record and the reference it came from.</li>
    <li><a href={REPO + "/blob/main/data/direct-line.tsv"}><strong>direct-line.tsv</strong></a>
    — the ten generations, with the evidence for each link stated in its own column.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="small">Also in the repository: the page-by-page reading logs for the civil death registers
  (<a href={REPO + "/blob/main/notes/1833-death-register-progress.md"}>1833</a>,
  <a href={REPO + "/blob/main/notes/1834-death-register-progress.md"}>1834</a>,
  <a href={REPO + "/blob/main/notes/1835-death-register-progress.md"}>1835</a>,
  <a href={REPO + "/blob/main/notes/1836-death-register-progress.md"}>1836</a>), which record every act
  read, not only the ones that mattered — so that nobody has to read them again.</p>

  <h2>Currency</h2>
  <p>Every source above was consulted on or before <strong>8 September 2026</strong>. Nothing here is
  quoted from memory or from another family tree: each claim traces to one of these, or is marked
  <span class="chip">inferred</span> and reasoned out in the open.</p>

  <h2>What has not been read</h2>
  <p>Set out in full, with the reason in each case, on <a href={u("/open-questions")}>Open questions</a>.
  The short version: the two Brisbane immigration files, the Archdiocese of Benevento church records,
  the Arienzo marriage supplements, and the two un-scanned volumes at Benevento.</p>
  <p class="small"><strong>Correction.</strong> An earlier version of this page listed “everything on
  Antenati” as unread. That is no longer true and had become misleading: four annual civil death
  registers have since been read in full, act by act. What remains unread there is set out on the
  <a href={u("/antenati")}>Antenati</a> page.</p>
</Base>
